```
Stage 1 — LDAP Enumeration Detection
Event ID 4662 (Directory Service Access)
Requires: "Audit Directory Service Access" (Success) + SACL on the domain object

Lab query (host-specific):
```

index=* host="WIN-AUHSOB0S2PO" EventCode=4662
| table _time Account_Name SubjectUserName ObjectName Accesses

```
Generalized production variant (filters out DC machine-account self-activity noise):
```

index=wineventlog EventCode=4662
| where NOT match(SubjectUserName, "\$$")
| stats count by _time, SubjectUserName, ObjectName, Accesses
| sort - count

```
KNOWN GAP: local/high-privilege LDAP reads issued directly from the DC console were
not observed to reliably generate 4662 events in this lab, even with a correctly
configured audit pipeline. Treat this query as covering remote/lower-privileged
enumeration and directory writes, not a complete recon detection. See README
"Detection Gap — Stage 1" for full writeup.
```
